---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'June 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use — ContrastLab"
  description="ContrastLab terms of use. Acceptable use, accuracy disclaimer, intellectual property, and limitation of liability."
>
  <Nav />

  <main>
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section style="padding: 72px 24px 48px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-hairline); background: var(--color-canvas-soft);">
      <div style="max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto;">
        <p style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-violet); margin-bottom: 12px;">Legal</p>
        <h1 style="font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem); font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-ink); line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 12px;">Terms of Use</h1>
        <p style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-mute);">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Intro note -->
    <section style="padding: 32px 24px 0; max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <div style="padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; background: var(--color-canvas-soft); border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline); font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-body); line-height: 1.6;">
        Please read these Terms of Use carefully before using ContrastLab. By using the Service, you agree to be bound by these Terms.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Prose content -->
    <section style="padding: 40px 24px 80px; max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <div class="prose-content">

        <h2>1. Use of the service</h2>
        <p>ContrastLab is provided as a free, browser-based tool for checking color contrast ratios. You may use the Service for personal, professional, commercial, or educational purposes.</p>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Use the Service in any way that violates applicable laws or regulations</li>
          <li>Attempt to interfere with, disrupt, or gain unauthorized access to the Service or its infrastructure</li>
          <li>Use automated systems to scrape or extract data in a manner that places unreasonable demand on our servers</li>
          <li>Misrepresent the source or accuracy of results generated by the Service</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. Tool accuracy and disclaimer</h2>
        <p>ContrastLab calculates contrast ratios using the WCAG 2.2 relative luminance formula and applies the pass/fail thresholds defined by the W3C. We maintain this implementation carefully and test it against known values.</p>
        <p>However, ContrastLab is provided <strong>"as is"</strong>, without warranty of any kind. We do not guarantee that the Service is free of errors, that results will meet every use case, or that the tool reflects the most current version of accessibility standards at all times.</p>
        <div style="padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; border-left: 3px solid var(--color-warning); background: var(--color-warning-soft); margin: 20px 0;">
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-warning-deep); line-height: 1.6;">
            <strong>Compliance disclaimer:</strong> Contrast ratio results from ContrastLab are a useful signal, not a legal determination. Whether a specific implementation meets accessibility regulations (such as the ADA, Section 508, EN 301 549, or AODA) depends on many factors beyond contrast alone. If you require a formal accessibility audit or compliance certification, consult a qualified accessibility specialist.
          </p>
        </div>
        <p>You are responsible for how you interpret and act on the results provided by this tool.</p>

        <h2>3. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>The ContrastLab name, logo, and original content on this website are the property of ContrastLab and may not be reproduced without permission.</p>
        <p>The underlying color mathematics used in this tool is based on publicly available W3C specifications and open standards. The WCAG guidelines themselves are published by the W3C under their document license.</p>

        <h2>4. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, ContrastLab and its maintainers shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising out of or related to your use of the Service, including but not limited to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Decisions made based on contrast ratio results</li>
          <li>Accessibility failures in products where ContrastLab was used as a checking tool</li>
          <li>Loss of saved data due to browser storage being cleared</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Your use of the Service is at your own risk.</p>

        <h2>5. Third-party services</h2>
        <p>The Service may include links to third-party websites or display content from third-party services (such as advertising). These third parties have their own terms of service and privacy policies. ContrastLab is not responsible for the practices of any third party.</p>

        <h2>6. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>We may update these Terms at any time. When we do, we will update the "Last updated" date at the top of this page. Your continued use of the Service after changes are posted constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.</p>
        <p>If changes are material, we will make reasonable efforts to notify users through a notice on the website.</p>

        <h2>7. Governing law</h2>
        <p>These Terms are governed by and construed in accordance with applicable laws. Any disputes arising from these Terms or your use of the Service shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts in the applicable jurisdiction.</p>

        <h2>8. Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about these Terms? Email us at <a href="mailto:support@contrastlab.com">support@contrastlab.com</a>.</p>

      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose-content {
    color: var(--color-body);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .prose-content p {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .prose-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-top: 40px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    padding-bottom: 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
  }

  .prose-content ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .prose-content li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .prose-content a {
    color: var(--color-link);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-link-bg-soft);
  }

  .prose-content a:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-link);
  }

  .prose-content strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
